# =============================================================================
# Almira — production environment.
#
#   cp .env.production.example .env.production
#   # fill in every value marked REQUIRED, then:
#   docker compose -f deploy/docker-compose.prod.yml --env-file .env.production up -d
#
# .env.production is git-ignored. Nothing in this file is a real secret; if a
# value here ever becomes one, it belongs in a secrets manager instead and this
# file should reference it rather than hold it.
#
# Generate secrets with:
#   openssl rand -base64 48    # JWT signing secret
#   openssl rand -base64 32    # key-encryption key (must decode to exactly 32 bytes)
#   openssl rand -base64 24    # database and Redis passwords
#
# One parsing quirk worth knowing, because it bites quietly: docker compose does
# NOT strip a trailing comment from a value line. `KEY=value   # note` sets the
# value to "value   # note". Every comment here is therefore on its own line,
# and yours should be too.
# =============================================================================

# --- Database ----------------------------------------------------------------
# Two roles, on purpose. `owner` runs migrations and owns the schema; `app`
# serves every request and CANNOT bypass row-level security. Never point both at
# the same user — /health will tell you if you did.
ALMIRA_DB_NAME=almira
ALMIRA_DB_OWNER_USER=almira
# REQUIRED — no default, and the stack will not start without it.
ALMIRA_DB_OWNER_PASSWORD=
ALMIRA_DB_APP_USER=almira_app
# REQUIRED
ALMIRA_DB_APP_PASSWORD=

# Only when using a database outside this compose file (RDS, Cloud SQL, Neon…).
# The compose stack builds this itself from ALMIRA_DB_NAME.
# ALMIRA_DB_URL=jdbc:postgresql://db.internal:5432/almira?sslmode=require

# --- Redis -------------------------------------------------------------------
# Holds one-time codes and rate-limit counters. Nothing durable, but a code
# store anybody can read is a sign-in anybody can complete.
# REQUIRED
ALMIRA_REDIS_PASSWORD=
# ALMIRA_REDIS_HOST=redis
# ALMIRA_REDIS_PORT=6379

# --- Sessions ----------------------------------------------------------------
# Signs access and refresh tokens. Rotating it signs everybody out, which is
# also how you respond to a suspected leak.
# REQUIRED — openssl rand -base64 48
ALMIRA_JWT_SECRET=
# ALMIRA_JWT_ACCESS_TTL=15m
# ALMIRA_JWT_REFRESH_TTL=30d

# --- Encryption --------------------------------------------------------------
# The key-encryption key that wraps every household's data key. Account numbers,
# policy numbers and document contents are unreadable without it — including to
# you. Losing it loses that data; there is no recovery, and that is the point.
#
# `local` reads the key from ALMIRA_KMS_MASTER_KEY. It is the seam a managed KMS
# plugs into (see crypto/KeyManagement): with `aws`/`gcp` the key never leaves
# the KMS and ALMIRA_KMS_KEY_ID names it instead.
#
# The application REFUSES TO START in production without a key. That is
# deliberate: a deploy that "works" while protecting data with a key nobody
# chose is worse than one that will not start.
# local | aws | gcp
ALMIRA_KMS_PROVIDER=local
# REQUIRED for local — openssl rand -base64 32
ALMIRA_KMS_MASTER_KEY=
# REQUIRED for aws/gcp — the KMS key ARN or resource name
ALMIRA_KMS_KEY_ID=

# --- Environment -------------------------------------------------------------
# Anything other than `development` makes the signing-secret, encryption-key and
# page-checksum checks strict, and stops the log code sender working at all. The
# compose file sets this; do not override it to `development` on a host anybody
# else can reach — that returns every one-time code to whoever asks for it.
ALMIRA_ENV=production

# --- One-time codes (sign-in) ------------------------------------------------
# `log` is the ONLY sender implemented today, and it works only in development.
# With ALMIRA_ENV=production every code request is refused with 503
# `otp_unavailable` and no code is generated: a deployment cannot sign anybody
# in until a real SMS sender exists. This file used to call `log` workable for a
# closed alpha; it was a sign-in for any number — see docs/17 §5, which also
# covers the DLT registration real SMS needs in India. Earlier versions of this file listed TWILIO_* and MSG91_*
# variables here; no code ever read them, so setting them did nothing at all.
# No SMS provider has been chosen yet — when one is, its credentials go in the
# ALMIRA_PROVIDER_SMS_* block below, not in provider-specific names.
ALMIRA_OTP_PROVIDER=log
# Sign-in attempts allowed per network per hour. Raise it only if a whole
# office shares one address; it is the defence against sign-in stuffing.
# ALMIRA_OTP_MAX_PER_IP_PER_HOUR=20
# Wrong codes allowed per network per hour, across every number. Successful
# sign-ins do not count toward it.
# ALMIRA_OTP_MAX_VERIFY_FAILURES_PER_IP_PER_HOUR=30

# --- Sign-in channels (closed alpha) -----------------------------------------
# phone | email | phone,email. The closed alpha is email ALONE: with both on,
# one person can sign in once by number and once by address and end up with
# two accounts nothing joins. Unset means phone, which is what every
# development tool expects.
# ALMIRA_SIGN_IN_CHANNELS=email
#
# The only addresses that can sign in by email, comma-separated. Trimmed and
# lower-cased; dots and +tags are kept as typed, so list the exact address the
# tester will type. No wildcard. Empty with email enabled refuses to start.
# Somebody not on the list is told a code was sent, and none is: the answer
# must not reveal who is in the alpha. Removing an address ends that tester's
# sessions too, at the next restart or their next request (known-issues 14).
#
# Email codes need an email provider that can deliver. There is no live email
# adapter yet (docs/13 §5), and outside development the sandbox cannot deliver,
# so today every email code request is refused with 503 otp_unavailable until
# one is written — the same honest refusal as SMS. Email in the channels with
# ALMIRA_PROVIDER_EMAIL_MODE=disabled refuses to start, naming both settings.
# ALMIRA_ALPHA_EMAIL_ALLOWLIST=
#
# Passkeys stay off until BOTH are set. A passkey is bound to its domain for
# good, so set the domain people will use and its exact origin. The
# authenticator app and recovery codes do not depend on these.
# ALMIRA_WEBAUTHN_RP_ID=almira.example.in
# ALMIRA_WEBAUTHN_ORIGINS=https://almira.example.in
# ALMIRA_WEBAUTHN_RP_NAME=Almira
#
# deploy/docker-compose.prod.yml passes both of these through, with the
# ALMIRA_PROVIDER_SMS_*, _EMAIL_* and _PUSH_* blocks below, by name only: a value
# left commented out here stays unset in the container and the application's
# default applies. A variable the compose file does not name does nothing.

# --- Notifications -----------------------------------------------------------
# Deliberately a logging stand-in until provider accounts exist. Every outbound
# message is recorded in `outbound_messages` either way, so the in-app list
# works and nothing is silently dropped (docs/13).
# Only `log` is implemented. This file used to say `log | sandbox | live`; the
# code has no other value, and per-channel modes live in the block below.
ALMIRA_NOTIFY_PROVIDER=log

# --- Outside services --------------------------------------------------------
# Each is disabled, sandbox or live. Every one defaults to sandbox except aa,
# which defaults to disabled, and `sandbox` here means OUR OWN in-process
# fake — none of them calls a real provider.
#
# `disabled` means not offered on this server, and starts normally: the status
# endpoint reports DISABLED, every call answers 409 provider_disabled, and a
# disabled sms/email/push channel is skipped. `off` is refused — write disabled.
#
# Setting any of these to `live` REFUSES TO START today: no live adapter exists
# for any of them yet. That refusal is deliberate and names what is missing.
# docs/13 records, per provider, whether its real sandbox is reachable now or
# needs partner onboarding first. In short:
#   whatsapp, push (Android)   a real provider sandbox is self-serve
#   email                      self-serve, once a provider is chosen
#   sms                        API reachable once a provider is chosen;
#                              delivery needs India DLT registration
#   push (iOS)                 needs a paid Apple Developer membership
#   digilocker                 has no sandbox at all; needs a GSTN-verified
#                              entity on API Setu and a server in India
#   aa                         CUT FROM V1 (disabled by default): needs a
#                              regulated entity (RBI/SEBI/IRDAI/PFRDA)
#
# Credentials only ever come from here. Timeouts are per call; attempts are in
# total, so 1 disables retrying.
# ALMIRA_PROVIDER_SMS_MODE=sandbox
# ALMIRA_PROVIDER_SMS_BASE_URL=
# ALMIRA_PROVIDER_SMS_API_KEY=
# ALMIRA_PROVIDER_SMS_SENDER_ID=           # DLT-registered header
# ALMIRA_PROVIDER_SMS_TEMPLATE_ID=         # DLT-registered template id
# ALMIRA_PROVIDER_SMS_TIMEOUT=10s
# ALMIRA_PROVIDER_SMS_MAX_ATTEMPTS=3
# ALMIRA_PROVIDER_SMS_RETRY_BACKOFF=500ms
#
# ALMIRA_PROVIDER_EMAIL_MODE=sandbox
# ALMIRA_PROVIDER_EMAIL_BASE_URL=
# ALMIRA_PROVIDER_EMAIL_API_KEY=
# ALMIRA_PROVIDER_EMAIL_TIMEOUT=10s
# ALMIRA_PROVIDER_EMAIL_MAX_ATTEMPTS=3
# ALMIRA_PROVIDER_EMAIL_RETRY_BACKOFF=500ms
# Live email is any SMTP relay (docs/13 §5). Required when mode is live: host and from.
# ALMIRA_PROVIDER_EMAIL_SMTP_HOST=
# ALMIRA_PROVIDER_EMAIL_SMTP_PORT=587
# ALMIRA_PROVIDER_EMAIL_SMTP_USERNAME=
# ALMIRA_PROVIDER_EMAIL_SMTP_PASSWORD=
# ALMIRA_PROVIDER_EMAIL_SMTP_FROM=
# ALMIRA_PROVIDER_EMAIL_SMTP_START_TLS=true
#
# ALMIRA_PROVIDER_PUSH_MODE=sandbox
# ALMIRA_PROVIDER_PUSH_BASE_URL=
# ALMIRA_PROVIDER_PUSH_API_KEY=
# ALMIRA_PROVIDER_PUSH_TIMEOUT=10s
# ALMIRA_PROVIDER_PUSH_MAX_ATTEMPTS=3
# ALMIRA_PROVIDER_PUSH_RETRY_BACKOFF=500ms
#
# ALMIRA_PROVIDER_DIGILOCKER_MODE=sandbox
# ALMIRA_PROVIDER_DIGILOCKER_BASE_URL=
# ALMIRA_PROVIDER_DIGILOCKER_CLIENT_ID=
# ALMIRA_PROVIDER_DIGILOCKER_CLIENT_SECRET=
# ALMIRA_PROVIDER_DIGILOCKER_TIMEOUT=15s
# ALMIRA_PROVIDER_DIGILOCKER_MAX_ATTEMPTS=3
# ALMIRA_PROVIDER_DIGILOCKER_RETRY_BACKOFF=500ms
#
# ALMIRA_PROVIDER_AA_MODE=disabled
# ALMIRA_PROVIDER_AA_BASE_URL=
# ALMIRA_PROVIDER_AA_CLIENT_ID=
# ALMIRA_PROVIDER_AA_CLIENT_SECRET=
# ALMIRA_PROVIDER_AA_TIMEOUT=20s
# ALMIRA_PROVIDER_AA_MAX_ATTEMPTS=3
# ALMIRA_PROVIDER_AA_RETRY_BACKOFF=500ms
#
# ALMIRA_PROVIDER_WHATSAPP_MODE=sandbox
# ALMIRA_PROVIDER_WHATSAPP_BASE_URL=
# ALMIRA_PROVIDER_WHATSAPP_API_KEY=
# ALMIRA_PROVIDER_WHATSAPP_WEBHOOK_SECRET=
# ALMIRA_PROVIDER_WHATSAPP_TIMEOUT=10s
# ALMIRA_PROVIDER_WHATSAPP_MAX_ATTEMPTS=3
# ALMIRA_PROVIDER_WHATSAPP_RETRY_BACKOFF=500ms

# --- Market data (docs/13 §6) -----------------------------------------------
# Public NAVs, closing prices and exchange rates. OFF unless switched on: with
# these unset the server makes no request to AMFI, NSE, BSE or the ECB. Nothing
# about a household is sent — each is a plain download of a public file. A
# price the feed records never replaces a value someone typed in (docs/13 §6).
# ALMIRA_MARKET_FX_ENABLED=false
# ALMIRA_MARKET_FX_CRON=0 15 21 * * *
# ALMIRA_MARKET_PRICES_ENABLED=false
# ALMIRA_MARKET_PRICES_CRON=0 30 23 * * *
# ALMIRA_MARKET_PRICES_SOURCES=amfi,nse,bse

# --- Document storage --------------------------------------------------------
# `filesystem` (default) or `s3`. Documents are encrypted before either
# provider sees them. With `filesystem` the path must be a real volume that is
# backed up with the database — in the compose stack, the `documents` volume.
ALMIRA_STORAGE_PROVIDER=filesystem
ALMIRA_STORAGE_ROOT=/app/var/documents
#
# `s3`: AWS S3 or anything S3-compatible (R2, MinIO, an Indian-region store).
# Startup refuses without a bucket and region, with only one of the two keys,
# or when the bucket cannot be reached with these credentials. Leave both keys
# empty to use the SDK's default chain (an instance role). The bucket is NOT in
# scripts/backup.sh — version or replicate it on the provider's side (docs/17 §6).
# ALMIRA_STORAGE_PROVIDER=s3
# ALMIRA_S3_BUCKET=
# ALMIRA_S3_REGION=ap-south-1
# ALMIRA_S3_ENDPOINT=                       # blank for AWS; the URL for R2, MinIO…
# ALMIRA_S3_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
# ALMIRA_S3_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=
# ALMIRA_S3_PATH_STYLE=false                # true for most S3-compatible stores
# ALMIRA_S3_PREFIX=documents/

# --- Logs --------------------------------------------------------------------
# json (the compose default) or text. JSON carries no MDC and no exception
# messages, and scrubs emails and long digit runs (docs/17 §8).
# ALMIRA_LOG_FORMAT=json

# --- Data rights: the grievance contact (optional) --------------------------
# Named in every rights reply and on "Your data rights" (docs/23). Unset, the
# page says the contact has not been named yet. The response period must be 1
# to 90 days (DPDP Rules 2025, Rule 14(3)) or the server refuses to start; leave
# it commented rather than empty, because an empty value is not the default.
# ALMIRA_GRIEVANCE_NAME=Grievance Officer, Almira
# ALMIRA_GRIEVANCE_EMAIL=
# ALMIRA_GRIEVANCE_RESPONSE_DAYS=30

# --- Contact us (optional) ---------------------------------------------------
# Shown in Settings (docs/03 §1.6). Unset, the card says it is not set up yet.
# No provider is called: the app opens a wa.me or mailto: link on the phone.
# ALMIRA_SUPPORT_CHANNEL=whatsapp
# ALMIRA_SUPPORT_ADDRESS=+91XXXXXXXXXX
# ALMIRA_SUPPORT_REPLY_TIME=within one working day
# --- One-tap links (optional) ------------------------------------------------
# The public https address of this install. With it, an "I'm here" reminder and
# a yearly "still reachable" question carry a one-tap link; without it they say
# to open Almira instead (docs/27 §2). Nothing is sent anywhere because of it.
# ALMIRA_PUBLIC_URL=https://almira.example.in

# --- Image -------------------------------------------------------------------
# Pin what you actually tested rather than tracking `latest`.
ALMIRA_IMAGE_TAG=latest

# --- Deliberately absent -----------------------------------------------------
# There is no variable that turns off row-level security, no "admin sees
# everything" switch, and no way to disable the encryption gate. The privacy
# model is not configuration.
